greedycraft.tconstruct.funeral.text.1=§7§oTo those poor souls lost in grief... my deepest condolences.
greedycraft.tconstruct.funeral.text.2=§7§oLong ago, people believed that after death they would become wondrous beings with tiny wings.
greedycraft.tconstruct.funeral.text.3=§7§oWhere do we go after death?
greedycraft.tconstruct.funeral.text.4=§7§oLike a funeral without end, She mourns on in quiet serenity.
greedycraft.tconstruct.funeral.text.5=§7§oSome believe death is a new beginning — yet all that remains after dying is emptiness.
greedycraft.tconstruct.funeral.text.6=§7§oWe are all feathers on the wing of society — no single feather falls by its own will.
greedycraft.tconstruct.funeral.text.7=§7§oButterflies are meant to pollinate flowers, yet here there is not a single proper bloom.
greedycraft.tconstruct.funeral.text.8=§7§oA mourner bearing great burdens came to this place to redeem all souls.
greedycraft.tconstruct.funeral.text.9=§7§oA funeral calls for solemnity — not colorful, gaudy adornments.
greedycraft.tconstruct.funeral.text.10=§7§oKilling begets killing — an endless cycle.
